Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:29:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Remove phone number sitewide, rebuild Contact Us as a
 real form
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Removed the phone number (footer, contact page detail row, "Prefer
  a call?" CTA) and the "YC Cheng · Penang" contact-person line from
  every page. Footer heading changed from "Visit or call" to "Visit
  us" since there's no longer a call option there.
- Contact page's right-hand panel is now an actual form (Name, Email
  Address, Company/Institution, Country, Message, consent checkbox,
  Submit Inquiry) instead of a mailto-only CTA, styled to match the
  site instead of copying the orange reference design directly.
- Wired to Web3Forms (a free form backend, since this is a static
  site with no server) via fetch/JSON so submissions land in the
  V-Chip inbox without opening the visitor's own email client. Includes
  a honeypot field for basic spam filtering and inline
  success/error messaging.
- NOTE: the form's access_key is still the placeholder
  "YOUR_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY" -- get a free key at web3forms.com and
  swap it in, or the form will fail until that's done.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
